Subject: Join nod preloader workers before the final disc stream is released
Upstream-base: ebd80cac99b48a323200d84365e07a58cc27412d

The last Preloader previously detached its worker JoinHandles. Worker-owned
clones could then invoke an FFI stream close after nod_free returned and after
the host had shut down its I/O provider. Disconnect the request channel before
joining all workers; retain the fallback stream until their destruction ends.
The explicit shutdown path uses the same destructor. Recover a poisoned thread
metadata lock and do not repanic on an already-unwound worker. Builds without
threading retain their existing field cleanup.

diff --git a/nod/src/disc/preloader.rs b/nod/src/disc/preloader.rs
--- a/nod/src/disc/preloader.rs
+++ b/nod/src/disc/preloader.rs
